@startuml
!include ../../rixte/shortfall/style.iuml
title Executing set-targets cal/2000 p/none

participant ":MishMash" as App
participant "cmd:SetTargetsCommand" as Cmd
participant "settings:TargetSettings" as Settings
participant "changes:TargetChanges" as Changes
participant "updated:NutritionTargets" as Updated

ref over App, Cmd : Parse "set-targets cal/2000 p/none"

App -> Cmd : executeWithResult(recipeBook)
activate Cmd

Cmd -> Settings : get()
activate Settings
Settings --> Cmd : current
deactivate Settings

Cmd -> Changes : applyTo(current)
activate Changes
create Updated
Changes -> Updated : NutritionTargets(...)
activate Updated
Updated --> Changes
deactivate Updated
Changes --> Cmd : updated
deactivate Changes

note right of Cmd
  hasSameTargets(current, updated), a static helper,
  compares every nutrient of the two targets.
end note

alt updated equals the saved targets
  note right of Cmd : Return a note: Daily targets are unchanged.
else updated differs from the saved targets
  Cmd -> Settings : set(updated)
  activate Settings
  Settings --> Cmd
  deactivate Settings

  Cmd -> Cmd : build the confirmation text
end

Cmd --> App : result
deactivate Cmd
Cmd -[hidden]-> App
destroy Cmd

note over Cmd, Updated
  The recipe book and the active meal plan are not used,
  so an existing plan keeps the targets it was generated with.
  The result has status done when targets are saved
  and status note when nothing changes.
end note
@enduml
